# ESP32 Web Scope - carrier board netlist
#
# This is the authoritative connectivity for the carrier board. It is a netlist
# rather than a drawn schematic because a netlist can be checked by a script
# (tools/check_netlist.py) and a half-finished drawing cannot.
#
# Format:  NET_NAME: component.pin, component.pin, ...
#
# The ESP32 dev board plugs into J2. Only three of its pins are used:
#   J2.1  = GND
#   J2.2  = 3V3
#   J2.34 = GPIO 34 (input-only, ADC1_CH6)
#
# All three measurement peripherals (PCNT, RMT, MCPWM) read this one pin
# through the GPIO matrix, so no other ESP32 pin is connected.

GND: J1.2, R2.2, R4.2, C1.2, D1.1, C2.2, J2.1
3V3: D1.3, C2.1, J2.2
SIG_IN: J1.1, R3.1
DIV: R3.2, R4.1, C1.1, R1.1
VIN_PIN: R1.2, D1.2, R2.1, J2.34

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Circuit description
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#  J1.1 (signal) -- R3 2.2k --+-- R4 3.3k -- GND     5 V -> 3.0 V divider
#                             |
#                             +-- C1 100n -- GND     input filter
#                             |
#                             +-- R1 1k ----------+-- GPIO 34
#                                                 |
#                                          D1 BAT54S (clamp to GND/3V3)
#                                                 |
#                                          R2 10k to GND (pull-down)
#
#  Divider:      Vout = 5.0 * 3.3/(2.2+3.3) = 3.00 V     (safe for a 3.3 V pin)
#  Clamp current at 12 V in: (12-3.6)/1k = 8.4 mA         (BAT54S rated 200 mA)
#  Divider RC:   2.2k * 6pF = 13 ns                       (vs 12.5 ns resolution)
#
# For signals above ~500 kHz omit R3/R4 and inject 3.3 V logic at R1 directly,
# because the divider's 13 ns time constant is comparable to the measurement
# resolution and smears fast edges. See docs/DESIGN.md section 5.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Board notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# - 2-layer, 40 x 50 mm, 1.6 mm FR4, 1 oz copper.
# - Keep the trace from R1 to GPIO 34 short; it is the only signal path that
#   matters for timing.
# - Ground pour on both layers, stitched with vias around the input network.
# - No ground plane under the ESP32 antenna area of the daughterboard.
# - J2 is a 2x19 socket so the ESP32 board plugs in and can be replaced.
#
# NOT VERIFIED: this netlist has not been through ERC, DRC, or a fabrication
# run. It has been checked for consistency against docs/bom.md and for
# electrical sanity by the arithmetic above. Treat it as a design intent
# to be reviewed, not a proven board.
